*Heading
Simply supported planar beam (B21) with a circular section: frequencies and buckling
** L = 1000, r = 10 (I = pi r^4 / 4 = 7854, A = pi r^2), E = 210000, rho = 7.85e-9.
** Euler-Bernoulli: f_n = n^2 pi / (2 L^2) sqrt(E I / (rho A)) = 40.62 and 162.49 Hz,
** buckling load P = pi^2 E I / L^2 = 16278.
** ccx runs B21 as a 3-D beam, circular sections only as B32: abq2ccx adds the midside
** nodes, fixes DOF 3 on every node and holds the free twist (else a 0 Hz mode and a
** meaningless buckling factor) with DOFs 4-5 at the middle node of the first element: at
** an element end node ccx 2.23 would lock the bending rotation of a circular section too
** (f1 1.46x, buckling load 1.88x); at the middle node both are as with the twist free.
